      "headword": "last",
      "priority": 2,
      "category": "part-of-speech",
      "title": "Classify final last as an adjective",
      "problem": "In the last train, last modifies train after the article the and is the ordinary final-in-a-sequence adjective. The current determiner tag is inconsistent with the learner categories used for only and best. Cambridge lists this last use under adjective; there is no existing en last/adjective entry in the inspected core.",
      "suggestedFix": {
        "correction": {
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective",
          "meaningEn": "final in a sequence; coming after all the others",
          "meaningKo": "순서에서 맨 마지막의",
          "meanings": {
            "ko": "순서에서 맨 마지막의",
            "de": "letzter; nach allen anderen kommend",
            "es": "último; posterior a todos los demás",
            "fr": "dernier ; qui vient après tous les autres",
            "ja": "順序の最後の",
            "zh": "最后的；排在其他所有之后的"
          },
          "reason": "Use the adjective category for last modifying train after the article the."
        }
      },
      "sources": [
        "https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/last"
      ],
      "status": "applied; native-review-pending"
    },
    {
